papers.abstract:
We prove the sixth-symmetric-power case of Foulkes' conjecture. For every integer <i>b</i> ≥ 6 and every finite-dimensional complex vector space <i>V</i>, there is a $\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}
olimits (V)$-equivariant injection $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b V)\hookrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6 V)$.

For every finite-dimensional complex vector space <i>V</i>, we prove that the canonical Foulkes–Howe map $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a V)\longrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b V)$ is surjective whenever <i>a</i> ≥ 2 and $b\ge a(a-1)$. This gives a quadratic stabilization bound independent of $\dim V$.

We prove the integral scalar-curvature inequality proposed by Gromov. For every dimension <i>n</i> ≥ 3, there is a constant $a_n\gt 0$, depending only on <i>n</i>, such that $\displaystyle \int_M(\mathop{\mathrm{Scal}}
olimits _g^-)^{n/2}\,dV_g\ge a_n\|M\|$ for every closed connected oriented smooth <i>n</i>-manifold <i>M</i> and every smooth Riemannian metric <i>g</i>. Here $\mathop{\mathrm{Scal}}
olimits _g^-:=\max\{0,-\mathop{\mathrm{Scal}}
olimits _g\}$, and $\|M\|$ is real simplicial volume. The proof uses the nonnegative-scalar-curvature vanishing theorem of the companion paper on rational inessentiality.
